<title>CANADA: Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Feb 14.</title>
<headline>Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Feb 14.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Gas Association (CGA) weekly survey of Canadian natural gas in storage in billion cubic feet (bcf):</p>
<p>							 Pct Full  Pct Full</p>
<p>		 02/14/97  02/07/97  Pct Full  Week Ago  Year Ago</p>
<p>East	     58.81     72.91    25.29	31.35     15.8</p>
<p>West	     73.73     77.93    28.45	30.08     34.3</p>
<p>Total Canada  132.54    150.84    26.96	30.68     25.5</p>
<p>East-West division is the Manitoba/Saskatchewan and North Dakota/Minnesota borders.</p>
<p>East capacity 02/14/97: 232.55 bcf, 02/07/97: 232.55 bcf.  </p>
<p>West capacity 02/14/97: 259.11 bcf, 02/07/96: 259.11 bcf.</p>
<p>The Canadian Gas Association survey includes liquefied petroleum gas, all Canadian operators of gas storage and Canadian companies contracting gas storage in the U.S.</p>
<p>((--Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
</text>
